{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0GYU", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-sheaves-section-QC}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{example-computing-exts}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{categories-definition-presheaf}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:477e78ae2fe3edf6e66198eb2fc9eaf2553377b7253d1e86f66b7c02e0b84c48", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c440bb9b812905da94da70452109db079a0de6f967b0862da2605caa8fa2cabe", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe material in this section will be used to define a variant of the\nderived category of quasi-coherent modules on a stack in groupoids\nover the category of schemes. See\nSheaves on Stacks, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a category. We think of <MATH_0002> as a site with\nthe chaotic topology. As in Example <REF_0002> we let\n<MATH_0003> be a sheaf of rings on <MATH_0004>.\nIn other words, <MATH_0005> is\na presheaf of rings on the category <MATH_0006>, see\nCategories, Definition <REF_0003>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a1bbcc1edfbd0c6c94128457b49c9ac45dce252896626b5bce13f8722b93a3e7", "unit_id": "tag:0GYU:prose-0001"}
